  "reasoning": "The patient explicitly states they have been taking a medication and subsequently developed weight gain, food cravings, and increased appetite. This direct temporal link between starting the medication and the onset of new symptoms strongly indicates an adverse effect or side effect of the drug. While increased appetite is also a symptom of diabetes, diabetes classically presents with weight loss, excessive thirst, and frequent urination, none of which are reported here. Additionally, the explicit mention of ongoing medication use points directly to a medication-induced etiology rather than a primary metabolic disease. Therefore, the facts establish a drug reaction.",
